  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x2018;Resilient Communities&#x2019; project in Pibor County in South Sudan, implemented by Oxfam through ICSP will directly reach 27,000 returnees, internally displaced persons and host communities. Oxfam will partner with government and CSOs to ensure that these conflict-affected communities especially women and youth will have improved resilience to protect, adopt and absorb shocks from all forms of disasters through integrated food security, climate resilience, gender, good governance and peace building interventions.  .  OUTCOME: IMPACT 1: People experiencing poverty and most vulnerable to shocks, conflicts and crises have more sustainable and equitable access to food and livelihoods.  SPECIFIC OUTCOME:</narrative>
  </description>
